  "description": "Parsing a script-master text file. input.text is the file content (UTF-8), or input.bytes_hex the raw bytes. expected.rows are the data rows keyed by the trimmed header cells (all values trimmed strings; a missing key means the row was shorter than the header), or {\"error\": \"ResponseParseError\"} for a file that is not UTF-8 text or not valid CSV (a NUL byte). The delimiter is whichever of , | TAB ; occurs most in the first non-blank line (first 4096 characters); a tie goes to the first in that order; , when none occurs. RFC 4180 quoting; rows whose cells are all blank are skipped; a UTF-8 byte-order mark is ignored; with duplicate header names the last column wins; extra cells are dropped.",
